cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use kammcircle, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "kammcircle: a desktop motorcycle simulator built on Kamm's circle"
abstract: >-
  kammcircle is a desktop motorcycle simulator in Python and PySide6. It runs time-stepped braking, acceleration,
  countersteering and tyre-temperature simulations, and solves steady turns on Magic Formula tyres that slip and
  camber, on sourced data for the Royal Enfield Himalayan 450 and Scram 411. Every figure carries its provenance,
  and the physics is tested against published results.
authors:
  - family-names: Soltani
    given-names: Achraf
version: 0.10.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/achrafsoltani/kammcircle"
url: "https://github.com/achrafsoltani/kammcircle"
keywords:
  - motorcycle dynamics
  - vehicle dynamics
  - friction circle
  - Magic Formula
  - countersteering
  - simulation
